{
  "analysis": "Inclusion is the failing class (recall 0.27, 136/179 missed) and the misses are overwhelmingly small (median 33.7px vs 90.5px train median; low-size tertile recall 0.14). Round 2's inclusion plan used scale 0.6-1.4 (too big) and uniform weighting, so it only nudged recall up. The missed inclusions look like small dark vertical blobs/streaks and a few speckled clusters, matching sources 11, 106, 150, 287, 50, 131. Patches (recall 0.70) and scratches (0.68) are decent but still miss small/low-contrast instances (median missed 49.6 and 39.1px), so keep small-scale prefer_small pastes, with thin bright-line scratch sources matching the missed thin lines.",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 30, "patches": 10, "scratches": 10},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.3, "scale_max": 0.7, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [11, 106, 150, 287, 50, 131]},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 0.9, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 0.9, "target_pool": "any_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": [19, 20, 200, 201, 203, 193, 76, 91, 96, 103, 169, 170, 187, 191, 192, 35, 36, 37, 42, 43, 44, 57, 58, 72]}
  },
  "rationale": "Shift inclusion to the scale band that actually matches its missed size (0.3-0.7, prefer_small) using compact-blob sources, and give it the largest share (30) since it has 136 misses and is far below the others; cumulative 75 stays under the 105 cap and near the ~80 diminishing-return zone. Patches and scratches keep small-scale prefer_small pastes (10 each) to cover their small/low-contrast misses without starving the shared detector; scratch sources restricted to thin bright lines matching the missed thin scratches."
}

